sentences.l:
Then an island, low-lying, stretches out beyond the harbour,
of the land of the Cyclopes neither near nor far away,
wooded;

for no tread of men keeps them away,
nor do hunters enter it, who through the woods
suffer pains, ranging over the peaks of mountains.

At once curved bows and light spears, long-socketed,
we took from the ships, and in three divisions arranged
we shot;
